## Use Case for eu-ehds:RegistrationElectronicHealthData
Description: This example demonstrates the formal representation of the initial acquisition and digital 
onboarding of patient health data into a regulated Electronic Health Record (EHR) system under the European 
Health Data Space (EHDS) framework. Following the strict definitions of Article 2.2(g), the scenario models 
the entry point of data where a Healthcare Provider transforms real-world health observations into a digital 
format. The core entity is the concept eu-ehds:RegistrationOfElectronicHealthData, which serves as the active 
processing anchor for the transaction. The process is initiated as a dpv:Process, targeting the multimodal acquisition
of sensitive datasets which could include pd:HealthRecord for clinical history and pd:PhysicalHealth for biometric vitals. 
By using the specific eu-ehds term (a sub-concept of dpv:Obtain as verified in the DPV 2.3 hierarchy), the model reflects 
the technical precision required to cover manual entry, device collection, and the digital conversion simultaneously. 
To satisfy the legal requirement for Purpose Specification, the registration is linked to sector-health:HealthcareManagement, 
a specialised purpose from the sector-health extension.
